                                                    Who’s Employed in the Early Months of the COVID-19 Recession?
                                                </a>
                                            </h2>
                                                    <div class="article-authors-date">
                                                        <p class="article-author-by">by</p>
                                                        <ul class="authors">
<li class="author"><span itemprop="author">Keith Wardrip</span></li>                                                        </ul>
                                                        <p class="article-date">January 2021</p>
                                                    </div>
                                        </header>
                                        <p class="article-excerpt">This research explores changes in the employment rate from 2019 to 2020 for residents of PA, NJ & DE and finds particularly large declines for three groups of workers with no more than a high school diploma: Black men, Black women, and Hispanic women.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
